title: Start
position: 54,12
tags: tutorial beginning
---
// This is a comment. Yarn ignores it.

// Basic dialogue
This is a simple line of dialogue.
This is another line. Each line is shown one at a time.

// Character names
Guide: Hello. I'm the Guide.
Guide: I'll show you the main parts of the Yarn language.

// Variables
// Declare and set variables with <<declare>> and <<set>>
<<declare $player_name = "Adventurer">>
<<declare $coins = 100>>
<<declare $has_sword = false>>
<<declare $reputation = 0.5>>

Guide: Welcome, {$player_name}. You have {$coins} coins.

// String interpolation
// Use {$variable} to insert variable values into text
Guide: Your reputation is currently {$reputation}.

// Setting variables
<<set $coins = $coins + 50>>
Guide: I just gave you 50 coins. Now you have {$coins}.

<<set $has_sword = true>>
Guide: I've also given you a sword. $has_sword is now true.

// Options (choices)
Guide: What would you like to learn about first?

-> Variables and Math
    <<jump Variables>>
-> Conditionals
    <<jump Conditionals>>
-> Commands
    <<jump Commands>>
-> Functions
    <<jump Functions>>
-> Advanced Features
    <<jump Advanced>>
-> Once Statements
    <<jump OnceFeatures>>
-> That's enough for now
    <<jump Goodbye>>
===

title: Variables
position: 852,377
tags: tutorial math
---
Guide: Variables can store numbers, and you can do math with them.

// Math operations
<<set $coins = 100>>
Guide: Starting with {$coins} coins.

<<set $coins = $coins + 25>>
Guide: Added 25: now {$coins} coins.

<<set $coins = $coins - 10>>
Guide: Subtracted 10: now {$coins} coins.

<<set $coins = $coins * 2>>
Guide: Doubled: now {$coins} coins.

<<set $coins = $coins / 2>>
Guide: Halved: back to {$coins} coins.

// Modulo
<<declare $remainder = 0>>
<<set $remainder = 17 % 5>>
Guide: 17 modulo 5 equals {$remainder}.

// Boolean operations
<<declare $is_rich = false>>
<<declare $is_armed = false>>

<<set $is_rich = $coins >= 100>>
<<set $is_armed = $has_sword>>

Guide: Are you rich? {$is_rich}. Are you armed? {$is_armed}.

// Compound expressions
<<declare $is_ready = false>>
<<set $is_ready = $is_rich and $is_armed>>
Guide: Are you rich and armed? {$is_ready}.

<<jump Menu>>
===

title: Conditionals
position: 1692,377
tags: tutorial logic
---
Guide: Conditionals choose which lines run.

// Basic if
<<if $coins >= 100>>
    Guide: You have at least 100 coins.
<<endif>>

// If/else
<<if $has_sword>>
    Guide: You have a sword.
<<else>>
    Guide: You should get a sword.
<<endif>>

// If/elseif/else
<<if $coins >= 200>>
    Guide: You have at least 200 coins.
<<elseif $coins >= 100>>
    Guide: You have a decent amount of coins.
<<elseif $coins >= 50>>
    Guide: You have some coins at least.
<<else>>
    Guide: You're quite poor.
<<endif>>

// Nested conditionals
<<if $has_sword>>
    <<if $coins >= 100>>
        Guide: You have a sword and at least 100 coins.
    <<else>>
        Guide: You have a sword but fewer than 100 coins.
    <<endif>>
<<endif>>

// Comparison operators
Guide: Here are the comparison operators.
<<declare $a = 10>>
<<declare $b = 5>>

<<if $a == $b>>
    Guide: a equals b.
<<endif>>
<<if $a != $b>>
    Guide: a ({$a}) does not equal b ({$b}).
<<endif>>
<<if $a > $b>>
    Guide: a ({$a}) is greater than b ({$b}).
<<endif>>
<<if $a >= $b>>
    Guide: a is greater than or equal to b.
<<endif>>
<<if $b < $a>>
    Guide: b ({$b}) is less than a ({$a}).
<<endif>>
<<if $b <= $a>>
    Guide: b is less than or equal to a.
<<endif>>

// Logical operators
<<declare $sunny = true>>
<<declare $warm = true>>
<<declare $raining = false>>

<<if $sunny and $warm>>
    Guide: $sunny and $warm are both true.
<<endif>>

<<if $sunny or $warm>>
    Guide: At least one of $sunny or $warm is true.
<<endif>>

<<if not $raining>>
    Guide: $raining is false, so "not $raining" is true.
<<endif>>

<<jump Menu>>
===

title: Commands
position: 292,377
tags: tutorial commands
---
Guide: Commands tell the game to do something.

// Built-in commands
Guide: The wait command pauses dialogue.
<<wait 1>>
Guide: That was a one second wait.

// Custom commands
// Commands are defined in GDScript and called from Yarn
Guide: Custom commands run code in your game.
Guide: This one shakes the screen.
<<shake 0.8>>
Guide: The shake command is a GDScript method.

// Stop command
Guide: The stop command ends dialogue immediately.
Guide: Want me to demonstrate?

-> Yes, stop now
    <<stop>>
-> No, keep going
    Guide: Okay, carrying on.

<<jump Menu>>
===

title: Functions
position: 1412,377
tags: tutorial functions
---
Guide: Functions return values you can use in lines and expressions.

// Built-in functions

// visited() checks whether a node has been visited
<<if visited("Variables")>>
    Guide: You've already visited the Variables section.
<<else>>
    Guide: You haven't seen the Variables section yet.
<<endif>>

// visited_count() counts how many times a node has been visited
<<declare $visit_count = 0>>
<<set $visit_count = visited_count("Functions")>>
Guide: You've visited this node {$visit_count} time(s).

// Functions in conditions
<<if visited("Conditionals") and visited("Variables")>>
    Guide: You've seen both Conditionals and Variables.
<<endif>>

// Functions in expressions
// You can use functions anywhere you'd use a value
Guide: Functions work in math too.
Guide: floor(10.7) times 5 is {floor(10.7) * 5}.

<<jump Menu>>
===

title: Advanced
position: 1132,377
tags: tutorial advanced
---
Guide: These are a few more features.

// Conditional lines
// A line with a condition only shows when the condition is true
Guide: Lines can have conditions too.

You always see this line.


You have a sword. <<if $has_sword>>
You have at least 100 coins. <<if $coins >= 100>>

// Line tags
Guide: Line tags add metadata to lines. #speaker:guide #emotion:happy
Guide: Tags like this help with localization. #line:unique_id

// Markup
Guide: Markup lets you style text.
Guide: This is [b]bold[/b] text.
Guide: This is [i]italic[/i] text.
Guide: This is [color=red]colored[/color] text.

// Escape characters
Guide: Use backslash to escape special characters.
Guide: Curly braces: \{ and \}
Guide: Square brackets: \[ and \]
Guide: Backslash itself: \\

// Jump vs detour
Guide: Jump goes to a node and doesn't return.
Guide: Detour visits a node, then comes back here.

-> Show me a detour
    <<detour DetourExample>>
    Guide: We're back from the detour.
-> Skip the detour demo
    Guide: Okay, moving on.

<<jump Menu>>
===

title: DetourExample
position: 1132,602
tags: example
---
Guide: This is the DetourExample node.
Guide: When this ends, we'll return to where we came from.
Guide: Use a detour when you want to come back afterwards.
===

title: OnceFeatures
position: 572,377
tags: tutorial once
---
Guide: The "once" statement runs content only one time.

// Basic once block
// Content inside <<once>> only shows the first time
<<once>>
    Guide: This line only shows the first time.
    Guide: So does this one.
<<endonce>>

// Once with else
// Show different content on repeat visits
<<once>>
    Guide: This is your first visit to this node.
<<else>>
    Guide: You've been to this node before.
<<endonce>>

// Once if (conditional once)
// Runs once, and only when the condition is true
<<declare $is_vip = true>>
Guide: $is_vip is true, so you see this line once. <<once if $is_vip>>

// Inline once on dialogue
// Put <<once>> at end of line to show it only once
Guide: This line only shows once. <<once>>
Guide: This line always shows.

// Inline once if on dialogue
Guide: You have a sword, so you see this line once. <<once if $has_sword>>

// Once on options
Guide: What would you like to know?

-> What's your name? <<once>>
    Guide: I'm the Guide. This option won't appear again.
-> What does once do on an option? <<once>>
    Guide: It hides the option after you pick it.
-> How's the weather? <<once if $sunny>>
    Guide: It's sunny. This option only appears once, and only while $sunny is true.
-> Regular question (always available)
    Guide: This option is always available.

Guide: Use once for greetings, tutorial lines, and options that should only be picked one time.

<<jump Menu>>
===

